1
00:00:03,628 --> 00:00:05,338
You're not screwing
with me, are you?

2
00:00:05,797 --> 00:00:07,424
Mr. Vincent, 
I'm dead serious.

3
00:00:07,841 --> 00:00:09,592
As long as you're willing to join us and

4
00:00:09,676 --> 00:00:10,885
give us your loyalty,

5
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,303
salary's not a problem.

6
00:00:12,721 --> 00:00:14,389
Yes, yes, I'll 
take the position.

7
00:00:14,848 --> 00:00:17,934
Besides, the Eagles, 
they just fired me.

8
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,021
That's the dumbest thing they've ever done.

9
00:00:21,229 --> 00:00:22,355
Don't worry, Mr. Vincent.

10
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:24,107
My team is going 
to treat you

11
00:00:24,107 --> 00:00:25,608
with the respect 
you deserve.

12
00:00:26,776 --> 00:00:27,694
Thanks so much.

13
00:00:28,403 --> 00:00:29,029
Great.

14
00:00:29,195 --> 00:00:30,363
Looking forward to it.

15
00:00:31,197 --> 00:00:32,323
Yes!

16
00:00:32,490 --> 00:00:34,743
Ted Vincent is joining us as head coach.

17
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:35,827
And...

18
00:00:36,077 --> 00:00:38,955
I am adding him to our player roster.

19
00:00:39,247 --> 00:00:40,081
Just in case.

20
00:00:40,081 --> 00:00:40,707
Wait, wait, wait.

21
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:42,792
Why are you registering him as a player?

22
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:45,211
Isn't he supposed to be our new head coach?

23
00:00:45,587 --> 00:00:47,005
Plus, he's old.

24
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:49,507
Okay, do you remember about 10 years ago,

25
00:00:49,507 --> 00:00:51,176
there was a 
college quarterback

26
00:00:51,176 --> 00:00:52,427
who was phenomenal...

27
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:53,678
All-American...

28
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:54,929
His name was Ted.

29
00:00:55,346 --> 00:00:56,056
Of course.

30
00:00:56,056 --> 00:00:58,058
He broke his leg during the championship.

31
00:00:58,058 --> 00:00:59,225
If that hadn't happened,

32
00:00:59,225 --> 00:01:00,935
he'd have been a superstar by now.

33
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,189
Hold on, sis.

34
00:01:04,189 --> 00:01:05,648
You're saying 
he's that Ted?

35
00:01:06,107 --> 00:01:07,275
Yes, sis.

36
00:01:07,484 --> 00:01:09,736
I've already had him checked out thoroughly.

37
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:11,237
With him on our side,

38
00:01:11,488 --> 00:01:13,281
we're definitely winning the championship.

39
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:18,620
Boo!

40
00:01:21,539 --> 00:01:22,207
Hey, buddy.

41
00:01:22,373 --> 00:01:24,000
You know what NFL stands for?

42
00:01:24,334 --> 00:01:25,168
Not for long.

43
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:26,920
That's how long
you'll be coaching.

44
00:01:27,253 --> 00:01:28,838
Three close games 
in a row?

45
00:01:29,005 --> 00:01:29,631
Really?

46
00:01:29,881 --> 00:01:31,466
This is the worst team
in the division.

47
00:01:31,508 --> 00:01:33,384
There's no reason for it
to be this close.

48
00:01:34,719 --> 00:01:35,929
I'll fuck your cousin!

49
00:01:36,096 --> 00:01:37,305
Fuck, poor fucker.

50
00:01:39,474 --> 00:01:40,892
What the hell happened?

51
00:01:41,184 --> 00:01:42,977
You lost to a 
third-rate team?

52
00:01:43,478 --> 00:01:45,063
You were winning 
so easy before.

53
00:01:45,271 --> 00:01:47,315
They must have studied our plays.

54
00:01:48,233 --> 00:01:49,651
Every route 
was locked down.

55
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:51,820
We won't lose again.

56
00:01:52,570 --> 00:01:53,446
When Ted was here,

57
00:01:53,655 --> 00:01:55,615
he always changed our plays on the fly.

58
00:01:55,865 --> 00:01:57,408
We never struggled
like this.

59
00:01:58,201 --> 00:01:59,702
If he were here today,
we wouldn't have lost.

60
00:01:59,702 --> 00:02:00,995
Shut the fuck up, James.

61
00:02:02,205 --> 00:02:02,831
Ted?

62
00:02:03,873 --> 00:02:06,292
You mean that assistant who led victory last time?
